# .cursorrules — ARGUS Full-Stack Build v6.0

## Project
ARGUS: Production-grade financial crime investigation platform.
Backend: FastAPI + NetworkX + Faker (Python 3.11+)
Frontend: React 18 + Vite + Tailwind CSS v3 + D3.js v7 + Recharts + Framer Motion + Lucide React

## Architecture Rules
1. Decimal(str(value)) for ALL monetary amounts. NEVER float for storage.
2. NetworkX MultiDiGraph. NEVER DiGraph. NEVER undirected.
3. Iterative DFS only. NEVER recursive.
4. sorted() on ALL set/dict iteration for determinism.
5. Frontend: ALL data from real API calls. NO mocked data. NO hardcoded values.
6. PYTHONHASHSEED=0 for all Python processes.
7. NEVER import from src.core.a2a_interface (creates second FastAPI app).
8. All components reference CSS custom properties. NEVER raw hex in JSX.
9. Node IDs are ALWAYS strings in API responses and frontend state.
10. Framer Motion for all animations. NO raw CSS transitions for component enter/exit.

## Import Strategy (v5.0 COPY approach with constant remapping)
FORGE modules: import normally via sys.path (project root).
TRACER modules: COPIED into tracer_service.py.
Assessment functions: COPIED into assessment_service.py.

## Constant Remapping (v5.0 — CRITICAL)
FORGE → TRACER aliases in tracer_service.py:
  LAYERING_MIN_DECAY → DECAY_RATE_MIN
  LAYERING_MAX_DECAY → DECAY_RATE_MAX
  SPACY_MODEL_NAME = "en_core_web_sm" (local, not in FORGE config)

## Field Name Mapping (FORGE → TRACER)
  Edge: transaction_id → id, transaction_type → type (uppercased), timestamp: datetime → int
  Node: int ID → str ID, swift → swift_code, country → jurisdiction
  Node: risk_score (float) → risk_rating (str: low/medium/high)
  Node: entity_type: person → individual, company → business
  Evidence: body/narrative → content

## Design System — "Forensic Elegance" (LIGHT THEME)
Typography:
  Display: Instrument Serif (headings, page titles)
  Body: DM Sans (UI text, labels, paragraphs)
  Data: JetBrains Mono (numbers, IDs, amounts, timestamps)

Colors (CSS custom properties only):
  Surface: --surface-0 #fff, --surface-1 #f8fafc, --surface-2 #f1f5f9, --surface-3 #e2e8f0
  Text: --text-0 #0f172a, --text-1 #334155, --text-2 #64748b, --text-3 #94a3b8
  Accent: --accent-base #4f46e5, --accent-hover #4338ca, --accent-tint #eef2ff (indigo)
  Status: amber=structuring, violet=layering, rose=danger/mule, emerald=success, cyan=info
  Chart: #4f46e5, #d97706, #7c3aed, #059669, #e11d48, #0891b2

Layout:
  Max width: 1440px, sidebar 260px, card radius 12px
  Shadows: subtle, layered (xs through xl)
  No dark backgrounds. Lightest is #ffffff, darkest card bg is #f1f5f9.

Animation (Framer Motion):
  Page entrance: stagger 50ms, fadeUp (y:12→0, opacity)
  Card hover: scale 1.005, shadow elevation, spring(400, 25)
  Number countup: easeOutExpo, 800ms
  Graph transitions: spring(300, 20)

## Backend Rules
- Pydantic v2 with field_serializer for Decimal
- FastAPI with CORS allow_origins=["*"]
- Lifespan hook auto-generates graph on startup
- In-memory AppState singleton
- DecimalJSONResponse with json.dumps(default=str)

## Frontend Rules
- @/ alias for src/ directory (clean imports)
- useQuery hook for ALL data fetching (dedup + cache)
- ErrorCard with retry on all pages
- Skeleton loading states (shimmer)
- No console.log in production code
- Canvas renderer for D3 graph (not SVG) at 500+ nodes

## Detection Rules
- Structuring: BFS fan-in, [$9K-$9.8K] USD, 10+ in 48hr
- Layering: Iterative DFS, 3+ hops, 2-5% decay, 12hr max between hops
- Currency isolation: group by currency BEFORE threshold
- Super-node skip: degree > 500
- Path explosion: stop DFS after 1000 chains

## Pipeline (8 steps)
receive → analyze → detect → synthesize → compute_confidence → draft → validate → submit

## Anti-Patterns (FORBIDDEN)
- float for money (use Decimal)
- nx.DiGraph (use MultiDiGraph)
- recursive DFS (use iterative stack)
- import from src.core.a2a_interface
- mocked/hardcoded frontend data
- dark backgrounds / dark theme
- bare except: (always specific exception types)
- list(set(...)) without sorted()
- import * (explicit named imports only)
- importing DECAY_RATE_MIN directly from src.config (use LAYERING_MIN_DECAY + alias)
- SVG for graph rendering at 500+ nodes (use Canvas)
- raw hex colors in JSX (use CSS variables)
- Inter, Roboto, Arial fonts (use Instrument Serif / DM Sans / JetBrains Mono)
- purple gradients on white backgrounds (use indigo accents with semantic color roles)
